Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||09-28-2001||09:48 AM||||To keep a retouched image looking real or 3D... you need to alter the color itself, but not remove ANY of the shading or highlights.  If you're using photoshop, you can create a new layer and switch it's mode from "Normal" to "Color", then adjust the opacity a little.  This way when you paint over the original color, it only changes the color- not the shading. The other thing you can try is adjusting the "Hue" of the image... this will often times effectively change the color- but not just of the car, the entire image. Hope that makes sense.<P>My Sig pict was enhance in PhotoShop (about 1.5hrs of work for final product) and has at least 6 or 8 layers (not including type). In PhotoShop layers are your friend!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000013||FLASHY||09-28-2001||10:32 AM||||You can manipulate the color of the car through "hue and saturation" in Photoshop. If you start changing the hue it will change all the hues BUT if you select a specific color at the top of the window (rather than leave it at "master" which is all the colors then it'll only change the color range you selected). For example, if your car was red, then click on "hue and saturation". Then at the top of that window select "reds" rather than leaving it on "master". Then slide the "hue" bar to whatever color you want. You can even saturate it more to give it a more metallic look. Just fool around on there for a bit and it'll make more sense the more you do it. Oh and the unfortunate thing is it won't work on white, black, or gray cars. It has to have color in it.<P>Hope that helps!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flash_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
